        "content": "<!DOCTYPE html>\n<html lang=\"en\">\n<head>\n<meta charset=\"UTF-8\">\n<meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0\">\n<title>Houses of Stucco — American Builder, July 1935</title>\n<script>\nwindow.MathJax = { tex: { inlineMath: [['$','$']], displayMath: [['$$','$$']] } };\n</script>\n<script id=\"MathJax-script\" async src=\"https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/mathjax@3/es5/tex-mml-chtml.js\"></script>\n<style>\n  body {\n    background: #2b2b2b;\n    margin: 0;\n    padding: 30px 0;\n    font-family: \"Times New Roman\", Times, serif;\n  }\n  .page {\n    width: 940px;\n    margin: 0 auto;\n    background: #fbfaf6;\n    padding: 55px 70px 90px 70px;\n    box-shadow: 0 0 25px #000;\n    position: relative;\n  }\n  .topline {\n    display: flex;\n    justify-content: space-between;\n    align-items: baseline;\n    font-size: 17px;\n  }\n  .folio { font-size: 17px; }\n  .running-head {\n    font-style: italic;\n    font-weight: bold;\n    font-size: 18px;\n    letter-spacing: 0.3px;\n  }\n  .kicker {\n    text-align: center;\n    font-size: 32px;\n    letter-spacing: 2px;\n    margin: 10px 0 40px 0;\n    font-family: \"Times New Roman\", Times, serif;\n  }\n  .headline {\n    text-align: right;\n    font-size: 62px;\n    letter-spacing: 1px;\n    margin: 30px 0 34px 0;\n    padding-right: 5px;\n    font-variant: small-caps;\n    white-space: nowrap;\n  }\n  .headline .of {\n    font-style: italic;\n    font-variant: normal;\n    text-transform: lowercase;\n    font-size: 46px;\n  }\n  .body-col {\n    width: 62%;\n    margin-left: 38%;\n    text-align: justify;\n    font-size: 19px;\n    line-height: 1.85;\n  }\n  .body-col p { margin: 0; }\n  .dropcap {\n    float: left;\n    font-size: 62px;\n    line-height: 0.82;\n    padding: 4px 6px 0 0;\n    margin-top: 2px;\n  }\n  .bullet { font-size: 15px; vertical-align: 1px; }\n  .logo-line {\n    margin-top: 75px;\n    text-align: right;\n    position: relative;\n    font-size: 56px;\n    font-variant: small-caps;\n    letter-spacing: 1px;\n    white-space: nowrap;\n  }\n  .logo-line .script {\n    font-family: \"Brush Script MT\", \"Segoe Script\", cursive;\n    font-variant: normal;\n    font-style: italic;\n    font-size: 46px;\n    letter-spacing: 0;\n  }\n  .sup-num {\n    position: absolute;\n    right: 0;\n    top: -18px;\n    font-size: 13px;\n    font-variant: normal;\n    letter-spacing: 0;\n  }\n  .subline {\n    text-align: right;\n    font-size: 27px;\n    letter-spacing: 6px;\n    margin-top: 6px;\n    font-weight: bold;\n  }\n  .lower {\n    display: flex;\n    align-items: flex-start;\n    margin-top: 40px;\n  }\n  .placeholder {\n    width: 560px;\n    height: 490px;\n    background: #d8d5cd;\n    border: 1px solid #999;\n    color: #444;\n    display: flex;\n    align-items: center;\n    justify-content: center;\n    text-align: center;\n    font-size: 15px;\n    font-style: italic;\n  }\n  .caption-col {\n    width: 210px;\n    margin-left: 60px;\n    font-size: 15.5px;\n    line-height: 1.75;\n    font-weight: bold;\n  }\n  .dot {\n    text-align: center;\n    font-size: 30px;\n    margin: 20px 0 55px 0;\n    line-height: 1;\n  }\n</style>\n</head>\n<body>\n<div class=\"page\">\n\n  <div class=\"topline\">\n    <div class=\"folio\">18</div>\n    <div class=\"running-head\">American Builder, July 1935.</div>\n  </div>\n\n  <div class=\"kicker\">PLEASANT &bull; COLORFUL &bull; STURDY &bull; ECONOMICAL</div>\n\n  <div class=\"headline\">H<span style=\"font-size:48px\">OUSES</span> <span class=\"of\">of</span> S<span style=\"font-size:48px\">TUCCO</span></div>\n\n  <div class=\"body-col\">\n    <p><span class=\"dropcap\">N</span>EW homes are selling. Modernized homes are selling. And homes finished in attractive, eye-inviting stucco are well up in the <em>profitable</em> sales parade. <span class=\"bullet\">&#9679;</span> Stucco as it is made and applied under today's specifications (and did you know that much of it is now <em>factory-prepared?</em>) is a finish particularly fitted to home building&mdash;both for new construction and for modernizing. <span class=\"bullet\">&#9679;</span> First of all, portland cement stucco is a durable, strong finish&mdash;actually it is a thin wall of concrete, and is comparably permanent, weatherproof and fire-resistant. <span class=\"bullet\">&#9679;</span> Second, stucco is applied in any texture suited to the architectural design&mdash;floated to a smooth finish, troweled in various semi-smooth effects, tooled, stippled, spatter-dashed, rough torn, or treated in other pleasing ways. <span class=\"bullet\">&#9679;</span> Third, with a finish coat made with <em>white</em> portland cement, <em>any color</em> is available in stucco&mdash;from pure white, through pastel tints of cream and salmon and tan and pink, to rich warm yellows and browns and greens and other shades. <span class=\"bullet\">&#9679;</span> Durability, texture, color&mdash;these are selling points for stucco that help convince your prospects of a home's desirability&mdash;and that mean ready turnover and profit to you. Want the details? Write Universal Atlas Cement Co. (<em>United States Steel Corporation Subsidiary</em>), 208 South LaSalle Street, Chicago.</p>\n  </div>\n\n  <div class=\"logo-line\">\n    <span class=\"sup-num\">210</span>\n    S<span style=\"font-size:44px\">TUCCO</span> <span class=\"script\">made with</span> A<span style=\"font-size:44px\">TLAS</span> W<span style=\"font-size:44px\">HITE</span>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"subline\">PORTLAND CEMENT</div>\n\n  <div class=\"lower\">\n    <div class=\"placeholder\">[Photograph: stucco house with striped awnings, arched front door and front steps &mdash; bottom-left]</div>\n    <div class=\"caption-col\">\n      <div class=\"dot\">&#9679;</div>\n      This trim and tidy home has been modernized with an Atlas White portland cement stucco finish in a semi-rough texture.\n    </div>\n  </div>\n\n</div>\n</body>\n</html>"
